/*
class Node{
    int data;
    Node left,right;

    Node(int key)
    {
        data = key;
        left = right = null;
    }
}
*/

class Solution {
    public boolean isSumProperty(Node root) {
    
        if(root == null){ return true; }                                      // Base case: null tree is valid
        if(root.left == null && root.right == null){
            return true;                                                      // Leaf node is always valid
        }
        
        
        int sum = 0;
        
        if(root.left != null){ sum += root.left.data;}                        // Add left child data if exists
        if(root.right != null){ sum += root.right.data;}                      // Add right child data if exists
        
        return ((root.data == sum) && isSumProperty(root.left) && isSumProperty(root.right)); // Check current + recurse
    }
}

//////////////////////// DRY RUN /////////////////////////////

Example 1: root = [35, 20, 15, 15, 5, 10, 5]
Valid Tree

        35
       /  \
      20   15
     / \   / \
    15  5 10  5

isSumProperty(35): 20+15=35 ✓ → recurse left, right
isSumProperty(20): 15+5=20 ✓ → recurse left, right
isSumProperty(15): leaf → true
isSumProperty(5): leaf → true
isSumProperty(15): leaf → true
isSumProperty(5): leaf → true
isSumProperty(5): leaf → true
Output: true

Example 2: root = [1, 4, 3, 5]
Invalid Tree

      1
     / \
    4   3
   /
  5

isSumProperty(1): 4+3=7 ≠ 1 ✗
Output: false

//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Children Sum in a Binary Tree
Given the root of a binary tree, determine whether the tree satisfies the Children Sum Property.
In this property, each non-leaf node must have a value equal to the sum of its left and right children's values.
A NULL child is considered to have a value of 0, and all leaf nodes are valid by default.
Return true if every node satisfies this condition, otherwise return false.

Examples:

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Input: root = [35, 20, 15, 15, 5, 10, 5]

        35
       /  \
      20   15
     / \   / \
    15  5 10  5

Output: true
Explanation: Every node equals sum of its children

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Input: root = [1, 4, 3, 5]

      1
     / \
    4   3
   /
  5

Output: false
Explanation: 4+3=7 ≠ 1 (root does not satisfy)

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Constraints:
• 1 ≤ number of nodes ≤ 10^5
• 0 ≤ node->data ≤ 10^5
